codex
The fetch job is still running quietly; I’ll let it finish on its own and then parse the saved XML, rather than relying on the titles alone.
codex
All 39 PubMed XML files are saved. Now I’m extracting only PubMed title, abstract text, and publication types from those local XML files so the verdicts are grounded in the fetched records.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "python -c \"import json, glob, os, pathlib, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
rows=[]
for path in sorted(glob.glob(r'C:/meta-harness/outputs/search_v2/verification/*/*.json')):
    slug=os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(path))[0]
    data=json.load(open(path, encoding='utf-8-sig'))
    items=data if isinstance(data, list) else data.get('records', data.get('items', data.get('rows', [])))
    for obj in items:
        if isinstance(obj, dict) and obj.get('verdict')=='ELIGIBLE_RCT':
            rows.append({'slug':slug,'id':obj.get('id'),'pmid':str(obj.get('pmid') or obj.get('id') or '').strip(),'nct':obj.get('nct'),'title':obj.get('title')})
def txt(e):
    return ''.join(e.itertext()).strip() if e is not None else ''
for r in rows:
    root=ET.parse(pathlib.Path('lane_x')/'raw'/(r['pmid']+'.xml')).getroot()
    art=root.find('.//PubmedArticle')
    title=txt(art.find('.//ArticleTitle'))
    abst=[]
    for a in art.findall('.//Abstract/AbstractText'):
        label=a.attrib.get('Label') or a.attrib.get('NlmCategory') or ''
        body=txt(a)
        abst.append((label+': '+body).strip(': '))
    pts=[txt(p) for p in art.findall('.//PublicationType')]
    print('\\n### {} | PMID {} | NCT {}\\nTITLE: {}\\nPUBLICATION_TYPES: {}\\nABSTRACT: {}'.format(r['slug'], r['pmid'], r.get('nct') or '', title, '; '.join(pts), ' '.join(abst)))\"" in C:\mh-r-X
